dogscoff wrote:
> YANI: 'Fearsomeness'

I really, REALLY like this idea. It goes a long way towards giving
monsters some common sense, which is one huge area in which I always
felt Nethack was lacking.

Some further ideas:

- Your size/the size of the attacking monster should also affect
fearsomeness. No newt wants to mess with a giant.
- Wielding a cockatrice corpse should dramatically increase your
fearsomeness (except for stoning-resistant monsters, of course.)
- Being blinded should change monster behaviour (essentially nullifying
your fearsomeness). Big, strong monsters will automatically attack you,
even if they can't see what they're fighting (what have they got to be
scared of?) while little monsters will panic and just run away.
- If a monster is "cornered", its desperation will override your
fearsomeness and it will attack you anyway.
- Demons always fight, no matter what your fearsomeness is.
- If a group of monsters is attacking you and one of them dies, this
should demoralize the others, decreasing their fearsomeness (in
proportion, of course. A dragon that sees a nearby newt die by your
sword is not likely to care, but if a newt sees that you can chop apart
a dragon, it will get out of there quickly.)
- Certain special roles - shopkeepers, nurses, priests, etc., will
always fight rather than run away.
- If you are polymorphed into something with a special attack (e.g.
cockatrice, dragon, etc.), this should increase your fearsomeness
against non-resistant monsters. Likewise, special-attack monsters
should have a high fearsomeness against you.
- Being burdened or worse should decrease your fearsomeness
accordingly.
- If a monster holding an object is overwhelmed by your fearsomeness
and turns to flee, there is a good chance they will drop the object to
placate you. (This would make dealing with nymphs much, much easier.)
- A monster with a wand of death, lightning, fire, or cold has a much
higher fearsomeness.

And many, many other things...I could go on and on, but you get the
idea. This is a very good idea, but there are many aspects of it which
would need to be taken into account.

I look forward to the patch!

Artemis the Ranger



